{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-integral}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4f82fa677d8ecc6a9679d2e2fab462083857e5a3e2719aac78404ce2fec091b4", "source_text": "Integral and finite morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d15c748af2dc4a20917caa30efd9e3206a30d72abb96ab8302ade46907ab1a11", "unit_id": "tag:01WG:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-integral-ring-map}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d837b3d6b58dd79f109efb1aa7f24f200a9d64a4b2d381acce1c697e97b71a35", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8bf0d29cf384c9b984f7e0f13c9d686f1c9926dbafa68a73a3b41b903be884df", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a ring map <MATH_0001> is said to be <TEXTITOPEN_0001>integral<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif every element of <MATH_0002> satisfies a monic equation with\ncoefficients in <MATH_0003>. Recall that a ring map <MATH_0004> is\nsaid to be <TEXTITOPEN_0002>finite<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0005> is finite as an <MATH_0006>-module.\nSee Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:34d2c437a9fe896291de03f11abc58cb46df1a0683f0c33d96fdf1b8b7e7543a", "unit_id": "tag:01WG:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(R) = V \\subset S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Spec(A) = f^{-1}(V) \\subset X$", "MATH_0006": "$R \\to A$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Spec(R) = V \\subset S$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Spec(A) = f^{-1}(V) \\subset X$", "MATH_0011": "$R \\to A$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-integral}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:22f31f0efc670778f6ecd8cdf64f95ede4b66a543756e0c91dddd91b1ed784ae", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:97947cfcea4f9e19465cc8ba2482d113a56489eadd7bb8500f5a7d87c7ebd4da", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say that <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>integral<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0003> is affine\nand if for every affine open <MATH_0004>\nwith inverse image <MATH_0005>\nthe associated ring map <MATH_0006> is integral.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say that <MATH_0007> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>finite<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if <MATH_0008> is affine\nand if for every affine open <MATH_0009>\nwith inverse image <MATH_0010>\nthe associated ring map <MATH_0011> is finite.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c5f3c3d03b1e63e9199a1c42aec4f724b26362187cdbd4ff459b44a321208673", "unit_id": "tag:01WH:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-integral-universally-closed}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd86694099739b7a10e015cc9db4f8c73d34773fa7d5b9dc711462d1546c7f3d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is clear that integral/finite morphisms are separated and\nquasi-compact. It is also clear that a finite morphism is a\nmorphism of finite type. Most of the lemmas in this section are\ncompletely standard.\nBut note the fun Lemma <REF_0001>\nat the end of the section.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4e55d40c6ecf78c7e2e516a3a999958a200905e4ad300e92744b99025aa9da64", "unit_id": "tag:01WG:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01WG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$S = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0004": "$f^{-1}(U_i)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_S(U_i) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(f^{-1}(U_i))$", "MATH_0006": "$S = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0007": "$f^{-1}(U_i) \\to U_i$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\subset S$", "MATH_0010": "$f : f^{-1}(U) \\to U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-integral-local}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b911e3f370ea2c149c95f7d1bc4212387797dab52c7ee6725f527d8db452349d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6ae334dc8a483b50ff884150d040d2008d85c9202ada8d4e1e290317135e607a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nThe following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The morphism <MATH_0002> is integral.\n<STRUCT_0003> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0003> such that\neach <MATH_0004> is affine and\n<MATH_0005> is integral.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an open covering <MATH_0006>\nsuch that each <MATH_0007> is integral.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0008> is integral then for every open subscheme\n<MATH_0009> the morphism <MATH_0010> is integral.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f6c1592b7a546e67bf3cc6ffb4577a18a6772827bfded5becb3def2029743e3", "unit_id": "tag:02K8:statement"}
